.TH LOSTC\-GUI 1 "2026-08-01" "lost-commander 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lostc\-gui \- dual-pane file manager, graphical
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lostc\-gui
.RB [ \-\-grid ]
.RB [ \-\-tree ]
.RB [ \-\-preview ]
.RI [ LEFT_DIR ]
.RI [ RIGHT_DIR ]
.br
.B lostc\-gui
.B \-\-screenshot
.I FILE.png
.RI [ LEFT_DIR ]
.RI [ RIGHT_DIR ]
.br
.B lostc\-gui
.RB [ \-\-help | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lostc\-gui
is the graphical view of the same file manager as
.BR lostc (1),
laid out for a pointer rather than a teletype: a sidebar of places, a
breadcrumb trail, per-pane views, and a real shell in a drawer along the
bottom.
.PP
Each pane carries its own view switch in its header \- a dense detail list, a
grid of large icons, the directory tree above its files, or a preview of
whatever the other pane is pointing at.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-grid
Start both panes in the icon grid instead of the detail list.
.TP
.B \-\-tree
Start the left pane with the directory tree above its files, which is XTree's
arrangement: walk directories above, tag files below.
.TP
.B \-\-preview
Start the right pane showing whatever the left one is pointing at, which is
what \fBF3\fR does.
.TP
.B \-\-screenshot " " \fIFILE.png\fR
Render a few frames, write a PNG and exit. This is how the view is checked
without a human at the screen.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
The function keys do what they do in
.BR lostc (1).
In addition:
.TP
.B F3
Preview in the other pane, following the cursor. With one pane it opens the
second to hold the preview and folds it away again afterwards.
.TP
.B F12
One pane, or two.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-1 ", " Ctrl\-2 ", " Ctrl\-3
List, grid, tree.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-G
In the byte editor, jump to a typed offset.
.SH FILES
The same as
.BR lostc (1).
The two front-ends share their settings, bookmarks and journal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lostc (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Alexander Garmash.
